","Sri Vijay Group of Institutions"],"about":"Sri Vijay Vidhyalaya College of Nursing and Research, Dharmapuri, was established in 2008 as part of the Sri Vijay Group of Institutions, governed by the Vijay Educational Trust — an institution with a heritage dating to 1986. Located at D.N.C. Compound, Gandhi Nagar, Dharmapuri, the college is affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University, Chennai, and recognised by the Indian Nursing Council (INC) and the Tamil Nadu Nurses and Midwives Council (TNNMC).\\n\\nWith the first B.Sc. Nursing batch having an intake of 60 seats, and subsequently adding Post Basic B.Sc. Nursing, M.Sc. Nursing and research programmes, SVVCN has grown to become a reputable nursing institution in Dharmapuri district. The college aims to provide quality nursing education, promote professional and personality development, and prepare skilled professionals to serve humanity in multi-specialty hospitals, government health centres and international healthcare settings. Graduates from SVVCN have gone on to serve across India and in Middle Eastern and Western countries.","highlights":["Affiliated to Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University","INC & TNNMC Recognised","Part of Sri Vijay Group of Institutions — Heritage Since 1986","Vijay Educational Trust","B.Sc. Nursing — 60-Seat Annual Intake","Post Basic B.Sc. Nursing & M.Sc. Nursing Programmes","Advanced Library with Foreign Books & International Journals","Clinical Training in Multi-Specialty & Government Hospitals","Qualified & Experienced Nursing Faculty","Separate Hostel for Boys & Girls","Active Placement Cell for India & Abroad","NSS & Community Health Activities"],"departments":[{"name":"B.Sc. Nursing","level":"UG"},{"name":"Post Basic B.Sc. Nursing","level":"PG"},{"name":"M.Sc. Nursing — Medical-Surgical Nursing","level":"PG"},{"name":"M.Sc. Nursing — Community Health Nursing","level":"PG"},{"name":"GNM (General Nursing and Midwifery)","level":"UG"}],"facilities":[{"icon":"ti-wifi",